Z||000000||ROB MAC||03-11-2000||07:57 PM||||Can anyone help?  Symptoms:  when headlights are turned on, idle drops intermittently, lights flicker, lights dim when brake is applied, static pop and zaps heard through stereo speakers (even when tape playing).  Symptoms disappear when headlights are switched off.  I've checked alternator, wires; both are fine.  I have new cap, rotor and plugs, recent battery.  I'm going to check the grounds; before I do, is there anything else I should be checking?||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||03-12-2000||04:12 PM||||checked the alternator how. have a full charging system check done with the car running. many places do it free. Sears, advance, autozone, pep boys, etc, all do it free.<P>check all the grounds carfully. There are several ground wires. the main ones your after are the 2 from the battery and the heavy block to fram one. check the thin + wire from the battery as well. ||||reg||1
