Z||000006||b_b_a_d||03-14-2000||01:52 AM||||Lack of power to your accessories makes me lean to the alternator... <P>However, stereo noise (crackling & popping sounds) bring me to ask when the last time you changed the RFI Noise Filter especially if you put in a HIPO ignition coil.  Sparks jumping to ground off your ignition coil, or damaged plug wires could be causing enough interference to affect other accessories.<P>RFI (radio frequency interference) Noise Filter is found in the same location as the ignition coil just to the right of it with a two prong connector and I believe a wire to ground.  Looks like a little cylinder about an inch or so long.  They run between $10 and $20 dollars depending on your source.<P>Good luck!<p>[This message has been edited by b_b_a_d (edited 03-14-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000007||Raydar||03-14-2000||11:33 AM||||You didn't say which engine you have. If it's a V-6, there are some grounds on the block, just above the transmission. They are directly below the throttle body. Easy (at least for me) to miss.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||ROB MAC||03-14-2000||08:29 PM||||its a 2.5 engine and wouldnt the clicks and pops be heard all the time if it were wires, plugs or coil and not just when the headlites are on? also the noises do not change frequency with idle or driving speed.||||reg||1
Z||000009||b_b_a_d||03-15-2000||01:17 AM||||I was just generalizing about interference from the ignition system.  Popping noises on the stereo made me comment on the RFI Noise Filter.<P>Did you check the voltage off the battery with a voltmeter under the same electrical load.  <P>Example:Car idling, headlights on, stereo playing, and heater/ac<BR> ||||reg||14
